# ResourceStat: steps from parity/shell_modules_resources_ResourceStat.qml.md (batches 1-5). Screen IRICE-TEST 1920x1080 scale 1;
# the island is centred at x 960 (closed y ~14, open ~392 wide); the bar is 30 px tall.
# Each block runs in both looks: the file runs top to bottom, Material first, then Glass.

look material
setup python3 -c 'import json, os;p = os.path.expanduser("~/.config/tessera/config.json"); c = json.load(open(p)); w = c.setdefault("desktop", {}).setdefault("widgets", []); w.append({"kind": "system", "size": "m", "x": 1, "y": 1}); json.dump(c, open(p, "w"), indent=4)'
wait 4
shot system-widget
note the desktop's System widget: each stat's name and value above a graph that fills over a minute (owner: desktop crate)
wait 3
shot system-widget-later
note values changed, the widget didn't flicker or reload

look glass
setup python3 -c 'import json, os;p = os.path.expanduser("~/.config/tessera/config.json"); c = json.load(open(p)); w = c.setdefault("desktop", {}).setdefault("widgets", []); w.append({"kind": "system", "size": "m", "x": 1, "y": 1}); json.dump(c, open(p, "w"), indent=4)'
wait 4
shot system-widget
note the desktop's System widget: each stat's name and value above a graph that fills over a minute (owner: desktop crate)
wait 3
shot system-widget-later
note values changed, the widget didn't flicker or reload
